#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.user.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Contact Email Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account contact information transfers properly via email integration.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate a provisioning contact last name
	* I rename the first user last name variable
	* I generate a provisioning contact last name
	* I rename the second user last name variable
	* I generate a provisioning contact last name
	* I rename the third user last name variable

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Krmail - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Mailkr - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prmail - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| MAILKRKRMAIL |
	| PRMAIL       |
	| MAILKR       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Krmail - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Mailkr - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Prmail - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| MAILKRKRMAIL |
	| PRMAIL       |
	| MAILKR       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Krmail - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Mailkr - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prmail - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Krmail - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Mailkr - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Prmail - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "provisioning-na-uat@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "provisioning-na-uat@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "New Liferay Project Invitation - Krmail - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "New Liferay Project Invitation - Krmail - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName3}" with the email address "pro.user3@lrpartner.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "New Liferay Project Invitation - Prmail - ${staticCompanyName}"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "¡Bienvenido al Soporte de Liferay!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "¡Bienvenido al Soporte de Liferay!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "provisioning-es-uat@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "¡Bienvenido al Soporte de Liferay!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "provisioning-es-uat@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "¡Bienvenido al Soporte de Liferay!"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "欢迎来到Liferay技术支持！"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "provisioning-apac-uat@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "欢迎来到Liferay技术支持！"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "欢迎来到Liferay技术支持！"
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "provisioning-apac-uat@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "欢迎来到Liferay技术支持！"

Scenario: View new contact emails
	Testing the ability to create a contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective new contact emails if the contacts do not yet exist in okta.

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Mailkr - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | ${staticContactLastName1}                  |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | ${staticContactLastName2}                  |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Krmail - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	#Necessary pause for email sync
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	Then I should be able to view the email message containing the following text 
	| Hi PRO ${staticContactLastName1}                                                                                                                                                                  |
	| Your Liferay Subscription Project Krmail - ${staticProjectName} has just been set up, however we were not able to locate your Liferay.com user account.                                           |
	| In order to gain access to Help Center, all of our downloads, and our support system, please create a user account with your company email address.                                               |
	| https://login.liferay.com/signin/register                                                                                                                                                         |
	| Once you have created and verified your account, please reply to this email and our regional provisioning team will gladly grant you access to the aforementioned Liferay subscription resources. |
	| Sincerely                                                                                                                                                                                         |
	| Liferay Support                                                                                                                                                                                   |
	When I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	Then I should be able to view the email message containing the following text 
	| Hi PRO ${staticContactLastName2}                                                                                                                                                                  |
	| Your Liferay Subscription Project Krmail - ${staticProjectName} has just been set up, however we were not able to locate your Liferay.com user account.                                           |
	| In order to gain access to Help Center, all of our downloads, and our support system, please create a user account with your company email address.                                               |
	| https://login.liferay.com/signin/register                                                                                                                                                         |
	| Once you have created and verified your account, please reply to this email and our regional provisioning team will gladly grant you access to the aforementioned Liferay subscription resources. |
	| Sincerely                                                                                                                                                                                         |
	| Liferay Support                                                                                                                                                                                   |

Scenario: View no new contact emails
	Testing the ability to create a contact in Dossiera and viewing that respective new contact emails do not get sent if the contacts exist in okta.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.user1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                             |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName1}       |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.user2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                             |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName2}       |
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Mailkr - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | ${staticContactLastName1}                  |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | ${staticContactLastName2}                  |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Krmail - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	#Necessary pause for email sync
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	Then I should not be able to view a support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"
	And I should not be able to view a support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName2}" with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "Welcome to Liferay Support!"

Scenario: View new contact emails for non okta user contacts in BR PT region
	Testing the ability to create a BR PT contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective new contact emails if the contacts do not yet exist in okta.

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Mailkr - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Sao Paulo                                  |
	| Address Country                        | Brazil                                     |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 04642-000                                  |
	| Address Region                         | São Paulo                                  |
	| Address Street                         | Rua Visconde de Porto Seguro 1238          |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | ${staticContactLastName1}                  |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | ${staticContactLastName2}                  |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Krmail - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay Brazil                             |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | Brazil                                     |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I update a user with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.user1                 |
	| First Name    | PRO                       |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName1} |
	And I update a user with the email address "pro.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.user2                 |
	| First Name    | PRO                       |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName2} |
	#Necessary pause for email sync
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "New Liferay Project Invitation - Krmail - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then I should be able to view the email message containing the following text 
	| Hi PRO ${staticContactLastName1}                                                       |
	| You have been invited to the Liferay project Krmail - ${staticProjectName}.            |
	| Access your project pages in Liferay's Help Center (pending confirmation) in order to: |
	| View your project's subscriptions                                                      |
	| Manage team members & roles                                                            |
	| Activate your Liferay products                                                         |
	| Learn how to succeed with each of our products                                         |
	| Search our extensive Knowledge Base                                                    |
	| Request help from our Support team                                                     |
	| We're excited to see what experiences you'll create with Liferay.                      |
	| Sincerely,                                                                             |
	| Liferay Support                                                                        |

